uns%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-review-279.png","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-review-279.png","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-review-279.png?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6"},{"sha":"c93049f83a496af7b43e80280ef2da1d95791eb6","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-readiness/source-scope-adjudication-v1.json","status":"added","additions":315,"deletions":0,"changes":315,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-scope-adjudication-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-scope-adjudication-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-scope-adjudication-v1.json?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,315 @@\n+{\n+  \"verdict\": \"quadratic-same-run-specialization-required\",\n+  \"scope\": \"Independent next-source-scope adjudication only; no frozen header/BODY authorization or closure\",\n+  \"actor\": \"/root/adaptive_reviewer\",\n+  \"requested_model\": \"GPT-6 Astra\",\n+  \"requested_effort\": \"medium\",\n+  \"runtime_attestation\": false,\n+  \"input_readiness_sha256\": \"dbc29a4da2ea3c0d77b4fe1f50e385edb5a1cd8cc50cabee41cbc0d313a1ca46\",\n+  \"exact_relevant_frozen_targets\": [\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Observing ell_t before output can make stability/gradient-square terms nonpositive; Section15.5.1.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"source contract\",\n+      \"status\": \"precise proposed target; external approval and proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          26\n+        ],\n+        \"source_anchor\": \"these terms become non-positive\",\n+        \"source_excerpt_sha256\": \"76eda1d8d1c97ff83f9937489bf8921f564a53627124d77755c51e991bb53c81\"\n+      },\n+      \"decisions_applied\": [],\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"repair:7.47-terminal\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"necessarydependency\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"For G_t=psi_t+sum_(i<=t)ell_i,arbitrary feasible z=x_(T+1) and finite displayed values, R_T(u)=psi_T(u)-psi1(x1)+sum_(t<=T)(G_t(x_t)-G_t(x_(t+1)))+sum_(t<T)(psi_t(x_(t+1))-psi_(t+1)(x_(t+1)))+G_T(z)-G_T(u). Mandatory labelled correction: retain real-round Algorithm7.8/hypotheses; define ghost psi_(T+1)=psi_T,h_(T+1)=0 and z in argmin G_T, proving attainment and all support/finiteness conditions. Then terminal gap<=0 yields printed sharp bound and Young bound. Repeating final hint instead requires adding h_(T+1)(u)-h_(T+1)(z), not cancelling it. The repeated-hint quadratic completion is refuted; no statement of equivalence to literal original is accepted.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"terminal statement correction\",\n+      \"status\": \"mandatory source-repair contract open\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [\n+        \"B4\"\n+      ],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"repair:15.31-terminal\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"necessarydependency\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"For BTRL with T>=1,proper closed lambda_t-strongly convex cumulative G_t,lambda_t>0,finite feasible played/comparator values and actual minimizers x_t, define ghost x_(T+1)=x_T. Prove R_T(u)<=psi_T(u)-psi1(x1)-sum_(t<T)lambda_t||x_t-x_(t+1)||^2/2+sum_(t<T)(psi_t(x_(t+1))-psi_(t+1)(x_(t+1))). Optional stronger endpoint is-lambda_T||u-x_T||^2/2. Original Algorithm15.9 defines no x_(T+1); repeating last loss gives checked0<=-1/36 and is not accepted.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"terminal statement correction\",\n+      \"status\": \"mandatory source-repair contract open\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [\n+        \"B4\"\n+      ],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-01\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Algorithm15.8: nonempty closed convex V subset X, strictly convex psi:X->R differentiable on int X, x_0 in int X, positive eta_t. Receive whole loss ell_t with V subset dom ell_t before choosing x_t in argmin_{x in V}(ell_t(x)+B_psi(x;x_(t-1))/eta_t), then pay ell_t(x_t).\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"retained later target; independent approval/proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-02\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Theorem15.30: additionally psi closed, iterates x_t in int X, losses subdifferentiable on V, nonincreasing steps. For every u in V: regret<=max_{0<=t<=T-1}B_psi(u;x_t)/eta_T-sum_{t=1}^T B_psi(x_t;x_(t-1))/eta_t. Constant eta: regret<=B_psi(u;x_0)/eta-sum B_psi(x_t;x_(t-1))/eta. The constant-step proof is explicitly left as an exercise and remains mandatory.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"retained later target; independent approval/proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-03\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Euclidean psi(x)=||x||^2/2 specializes the negative stability term to -sum||x_t-x_(t-1)||^2/(2eta_t), with no positive gradient-square term. The total bound need not be nonpositive because the initial comparator potential is positive.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"retained later target; independent approval/proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-04\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"optionalroute\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"The original BTRL15.31 contract is retained verbatim in archival_sources. Effective guarantee is repair:15.31-terminal with repair:7.47-terminal prerequisite; no unrepaired endpoint inequality is asserted.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"alternate route optional for C2 implication; already-inventoried theorem and its repair remain required/open\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\",\n+      \"scope\": {\n+        \"primary_chapter2_euclidean_implication\": \"optionalroute\",\n+        \"book_goal_required\": true,\n+        \"required_in_owning_chapter\": 15,\n+        \"scope_basis\": \"Retained source mathematics or mandatory source repair in the owning chapter; optional only as a route for the primary Chapter2 Euclidean implication. Existing source/repair distinction unchanged.\"\n+      }\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"conclusion\": \"Frozen later:lookahead/branch-03 asks for general quadratic same-run specialization, including variable steps, not merely an affine fixed-step example. Existing accepted generic Bregman source_fixed_regret/source_variable_regret already cover the literal Theorem15.30 and its mandatory fixed-step exercise conditionally on valid source updates. Existing OnlinePrescientLinear is a useful affine fixed-step instance but does not reconcile the generic nonlinear/subdifferentiable quadratic branch.\",\n+  \"minimal_required_math\": [\n+    {\n+      \"endpoint\": \"Shared quadratic Bregman identity\",\n+      \"statement\": \"For psi(z)=||z||^2/2 in the existing shared divergence definition, B_psi(a;b)=||a-b||^2/2. Use existing Mathlib derivative/quadratic results; no duplicate divergence or per-Book algorithm.\",\n+      \"role\": \"Reusable algebra/derivative bridge, no regret result by itself.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"endpoint\": \"Actual prescient quadratic variable-step regret\",\n+      \"statement\": \"For arbitrary source-compatible extended-real loss sequence, positive played nonincreasing eta, natural T>0, any u in nonempty closed convex V, and a valid run of the existing Option iterate with quadratic regularizer: sum_{t<T}(loss_t(x_(t+1))-loss_t(u)) <= max_{t<T}||u-x_t||^2/(2 eta_(T-1)) - sum_{t<T}||x_(t+1)-x_t||^2/(2 eta_t).\",\n+      \"role\": \"Same actual shared producer as source15.30; no affine restriction or assumed desired bound.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"endpoint\": \"Constant-step quadratic specialization\",\n+      \"statement\": \"Under corresponding fixed eta>0 conditions, regret <= ||u-x0||^2/(2eta) - sum_{t<T}||x_(t+1)-x_t||^2/(2eta). T=0 may remain supported as in existing fixed source theorem.\",\n+      \"role\": \"Retain mandatory fixed-step source branch; derive from already accepted fixed Bregman endpoint and identity, not reprove telescoping. May be bundled with variable endpoint; no forced public helper chain.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"source_hypotheses_and_information\": [\n+    \"Source losses exclude minus infinity globally and are finite on V (V subset effectiveDomain); retain nonempty support/subdifferentiability on V. Do not replace by globally finite differentiable losses or affine losses.\",\n+    \"Preserve source nonempty closed convex V and valid minimizer/run assumptions. Existing SourceProper can be derived from no-bottom/domain/nonempty rather than silently strengthened.\",\n+    \"Quadratic all-space ambient X=univ discharges interior/differentiability geometrically; explicitly label this specialization. For arbitrary X, retain source interior points and closedness/extension hypotheses instead of dropping them.\",\n+    \"Prediction is x_(t+1) after observing whole current loss t, unlike causal OGD pre-update scoring. Initial state Lean0 is sourcex0; loss0 is sourceell1.\",\n+    \"Use existing Option advance/iterate. Either conditional successful-run hseq or source hmin updates with proved uniqueness/iterate bridge is legitimate. No universal attainment or invented total selector; failure semantics remain none/absorbing.\",\n+    \"Negative movement-square stability is not negative ordinary-gradient-square for arbitrary constrained/nonsmooth losses. The total upper bound need not be nonpositive because comparator potential remains.\"\n+  ],\n+  \"reuse\": [\n+    \"OnlineBregman.divergence and existing derivative APIs\",\n+    \"OnlinePrescientBregman.iterate_eq_of_source_updates\",\n+    \"OnlinePrescientBregman.source_variable_regret and source_fixed_regret (or actual-run variants with explicit source-hypothesis transport)\",\n+    \"Existing Option selector success/failure specifications\"\n+  ],\n+  \"source_pixels_personally_reviewed\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-book\\\\tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-closure-readiness-20261011\\\\source-review-277.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"339f31ebcbcdd5d32faf6b4265b1fa24f136d16bb6196ccf57550e653996be76\",\n+      \"pdf_page\": 277\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-book\\\\tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-closure-readiness-20261011\\\\source-review-278.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"5389304af84a00a8f26aebb27fa3f0532193b40f87f0bd7f121a18a41865d613\",\n+      \"pdf_page\": 278\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-book\\\\tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-closure-readiness-20261011\\\\source-review-279.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"e0505deba7e5b566def310bc40c8b4f155f8af3dd339fc33fd00c6ea567b8dbe\",\n+      \"pdf_page\": 279\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"source_pdf_sha256\": \"cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17\",\n+  \"source_page26\": \"Personally inspected in earlier source-route reviews; current PDF hash pinned.\",\n+  \"accepted_module_joins_verified\": [\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientLinear.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregman.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanRegret.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanSource.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"B4_boundary\": \"repair:7.47-terminal and repair:15.31-terminal remain mandatory/open for owning Chapter15/global Goal. They are not prerequisites for this quadratic mirror-descent leaf; completion of branch03 does not close every lookahead target/container. Preserve explicit optional-C2-route versus owning-chapter-required scope.\",\n+  \"next_gate\": \"Formalizer prepares exact neutral header/imported-definition packet, fresh distinct blind decoding, independent source-contract approval before any proof. This adjudication does not freeze a header.\",\n+  \"current_counts_unchanged\": {\n+    \"forward_containers\": 8,\n+    \"future_claims\": 6,\n+    \"chapter_partial\": true,\n+    \"denominator\": null,\n+    \"Goal\": \"ACTIVE\"\n+  },\n+  \"input_raw_hashes_verified\": {\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-complete-target-freeze-v1/effective-targets-frozen-v3.2.json\": \"61cf1901a632aeee35ee71511ba53b115ae0958649ea78b786536a4404684ba1\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"aea107ead82743ae4c4948d64cbd9ba5b299dde77b2b1eeb1689cb0cabf8a0cf\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"3a990b8e99bc748484e7cce0dae96b3eb7de4e3607968cfe7f9067a17f301579\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientLinear.lean\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"45a146d80dd47330f7f2c74e13f3a4ade0ccfc0fb3c0c7acbc46a82e6255f3f4\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"6ec068dfcecf67fd9c8940e36e19db928510938b1da95fc4c4e22c0082852609\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregman.lean\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"01fcf3e5580e1afee0f5a26acc60393f429855458db35d02f888b99111fdc1bb\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"ae622824ac2ba49d90af62c065844c12c29a53a09689091243335e21ea6891fa\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanRegret.lean\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"651f566002add20400c62aacb5e6b84760358c127e3281f684e790643a53d00f\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"7d4b498c7bc28689427c342bcb4bdeeb86c433ce74baf0ad760651a863804d95\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanSource.lean\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlineBregmanProximal.lean\": \"8708aa5e15ff334ce8070cc976634ebaf8dc63314d3da95b502640f68350288f\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlineBregmanExtended.lean\": \"adf36bd3172a96308872323af3128fc94733c005ca9c025a050620804f7ed80b\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/six-BODY-review-v1.md\": \"be28bab8d9552cb88570346aee6b6a56c333842df382070ca6ee68ac1b40d717\"\n+  },\n+  \"created_utc\": \"2026-10-11T05:36:37.352239+00:00\"\n+}"},{"sha":"9c01c07c4227cfc7d9848886d65c3a6c353d1434","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-readiness/source-scope-adjudication-v1.md","status":"added","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changes":9,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-scope-adjudication-v1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-scope-adjudication-v1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fsource-scope-adjudication-v1.md?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+# Prescient quadratic source-scope adjudication\n+\n+The frozen branch03 requires a general same-run quadratic Bregman specialization. The accepted affine fixed-step result alone is insufficient. Existing generic source15.30 variable and fixed bounds, including the fixed-step exercise, should be reused rather than reproved.\n+\n+Minimal remaining mathematics is the shared quadratic divergence identity and its substitution into the actual conditional variable/fixed prescient regret bounds. Retain arbitrary source-compatible extended-real losses, finite values/supports on V, valid source updates or successful Option runs, and exact negative movement-square terms. The variable branch needs positive nonincreasing played steps and T>0; the fixed branch must not be replaced by a weaker maximum-potential statement. No duplicated selector or public helper chain is needed.\n+\n+Whole current loss precedes prediction; score the new state. Quadratic ambient X=univ discharges interior/differentiability as an explicit specialization, not by hiding assumptions. Do not assert total attainment, negative ordinary-gradient-square terms for general constrained losses, or nonpositive total regret.\n+\n+Personally inspected PDF277–279 original pixels and verified current accepted module RAW/HEAD joins. B4 corrected7.47/15.31 remains mandatory/open but does not block this quadratic leaf. Neither this proposal nor eventual branch03 completion closes the whole Chapter15 lookahead scope. Exact headers still need separate freeze/blind/source review; no proof or closure authorized."},{"sha":"33b5637b96207ab9fca3108262d203a6c3d29f65","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-readiness/v1.json","status":"added","additions":378,"deletions":0,"changes":378,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fv1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fv1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fv1.json?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,378 @@\n+{\n+  \"actor\": \"/root/adaptive_decoder\",\n+  \"role\": \"source-exposed independent readiness audit\",\n+  \"requested_model\": \"GPT-6 Astra\",\n+  \"requested_effort\": \"medium\",\n+  \"runtime_attestation\": false,\n+  \"status\": \"proposal-only; no acceptance or count change\",\n+  \"input_raw_sha256\": {\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-complete-target-freeze-v1/effective-targets-frozen-v3.2.json\": \"61cf1901a632aeee35ee71511ba53b115ae0958649ea78b786536a4404684ba1\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"aea107ead82743ae4c4948d64cbd9ba5b299dde77b2b1eeb1689cb0cabf8a0cf\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"3a990b8e99bc748484e7cce0dae96b3eb7de4e3607968cfe7f9067a17f301579\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientLinear.lean\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"45a146d80dd47330f7f2c74e13f3a4ade0ccfc0fb3c0c7acbc46a82e6255f3f4\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"6ec068dfcecf67fd9c8940e36e19db928510938b1da95fc4c4e22c0082852609\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregman.lean\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"01fcf3e5580e1afee0f5a26acc60393f429855458db35d02f888b99111fdc1bb\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"ae622824ac2ba49d90af62c065844c12c29a53a09689091243335e21ea6891fa\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanRegret.lean\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/FINAL-review-v1.json\": \"651f566002add20400c62aacb5e6b84760358c127e3281f684e790643a53d00f\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\": \"7d4b498c7bc28689427c342bcb4bdeeb86c433ce74baf0ad760651a863804d95\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanSource.lean\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlineBregmanProximal.lean\": \"8708aa5e15ff334ce8070cc976634ebaf8dc63314d3da95b502640f68350288f\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlineBregmanExtended.lean\": \"adf36bd3172a96308872323af3128fc94733c005ca9c025a050620804f7ed80b\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/six-BODY-review-v1.md\": \"be28bab8d9552cb88570346aee6b6a56c333842df382070ca6ee68ac1b40d717\"\n+  },\n+  \"pdf\": {\n+    \"path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-ogd\\\\tmp\\\\pdfs\\\\orabona-v10.pdf\",\n+    \"sha256\": \"cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17\",\n+    \"pages\": [\n+      {\n+        \"pdf_page\": 26,\n+        \"printed_page\": 14,\n+        \"extraction_path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-book\\\\tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-closure-readiness-20261011\\\\pdf-26-text-v1.txt\",\n+        \"utf8_excerpt_sha256\": \"d11025f870a83d9cec5011a5f101bce0d26cca5a6d9b61c1acb749071d40fefb\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"pdf_page\": 277,\n+        \"printed_page\": 265,\n+        \"extraction_path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-book\\\\tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-closure-readiness-20261011\\\\pdf-277-text-v1.txt\",\n+        \"utf8_excerpt_sha256\": \"3a7a542207648c22226c4a5310bd7b77ea59e10acc5aacaad8ec4cd9fbaf0b74\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"pdf_page\": 278,\n+        \"printed_page\": 266,\n+        \"extraction_path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-book\\\\tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-closure-readiness-20261011\\\\pdf-278-text-v1.txt\",\n+        \"utf8_excerpt_sha256\": \"81a9b2322b61cb62cba6628798e81d3e99107057dda69e5a7b16d07d34304630\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"pdf_page\": 279,\n+        \"printed_page\": 267,\n+        \"extraction_path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-book\\\\tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-closure-readiness-20261011\\\\pdf-279-text-v1.txt\",\n+        \"utf8_excerpt_sha256\": \"b44a96f194dce5812ae9d4b97b0dd0ed9946f900fe1556ecc35adbb627328b88\"\n+      }\n+    ],\n+    \"fresh_pixel_inspection\": false\n+  },\n+  \"exact_relevant_target_rows\": [\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Observing ell_t before output can make stability/gradient-square terms nonpositive; Section15.5.1.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"source contract\",\n+      \"status\": \"precise proposed target; external approval and proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          26\n+        ],\n+        \"source_anchor\": \"these terms become non-positive\",\n+        \"source_excerpt_sha256\": \"76eda1d8d1c97ff83f9937489bf8921f564a53627124d77755c51e991bb53c81\"\n+      },\n+      \"decisions_applied\": [],\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"repair:7.47-terminal\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"necessarydependency\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"For G_t=psi_t+sum_(i<=t)ell_i,arbitrary feasible z=x_(T+1) and finite displayed values, R_T(u)=psi_T(u)-psi1(x1)+sum_(t<=T)(G_t(x_t)-G_t(x_(t+1)))+sum_(t<T)(psi_t(x_(t+1))-psi_(t+1)(x_(t+1)))+G_T(z)-G_T(u). Mandatory labelled correction: retain real-round Algorithm7.8/hypotheses; define ghost psi_(T+1)=psi_T,h_(T+1)=0 and z in argmin G_T, proving attainment and all support/finiteness conditions. Then terminal gap<=0 yields printed sharp bound and Young bound. Repeating final hint instead requires adding h_(T+1)(u)-h_(T+1)(z), not cancelling it. The repeated-hint quadratic completion is refuted; no statement of equivalence to literal original is accepted.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"terminal statement correction\",\n+      \"status\": \"mandatory source-repair contract open\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [\n+        \"B4\"\n+      ],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"repair:15.31-terminal\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"forward:prescient-lookahead\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"necessarydependency\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"For BTRL with T>=1,proper closed lambda_t-strongly convex cumulative G_t,lambda_t>0,finite feasible played/comparator values and actual minimizers x_t, define ghost x_(T+1)=x_T. Prove R_T(u)<=psi_T(u)-psi1(x1)-sum_(t<T)lambda_t||x_t-x_(t+1)||^2/2+sum_(t<T)(psi_t(x_(t+1))-psi_(t+1)(x_(t+1))). Optional stronger endpoint is-lambda_T||u-x_T||^2/2. Original Algorithm15.9 defines no x_(T+1); repeating last loss gives checked0<=-1/36 and is not accepted.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"terminal statement correction\",\n+      \"status\": \"mandatory source-repair contract open\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [\n+        \"B4\"\n+      ],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-01\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Algorithm15.8: nonempty closed convex V subset X, strictly convex psi:X->R differentiable on int X, x_0 in int X, positive eta_t. Receive whole loss ell_t with V subset dom ell_t before choosing x_t in argmin_{x in V}(ell_t(x)+B_psi(x;x_(t-1))/eta_t), then pay ell_t(x_t).\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"retained later target; independent approval/proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-02\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Theorem15.30: additionally psi closed, iterates x_t in int X, losses subdifferentiable on V, nonincreasing steps. For every u in V: regret<=max_{0<=t<=T-1}B_psi(u;x_t)/eta_T-sum_{t=1}^T B_psi(x_t;x_(t-1))/eta_t. Constant eta: regret<=B_psi(u;x_0)/eta-sum B_psi(x_t;x_(t-1))/eta. The constant-step proof is explicitly left as an exercise and remains mandatory.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"retained later target; independent approval/proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-03\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Euclidean psi(x)=||x||^2/2 specializes the negative stability term to -sum||x_t-x_(t-1)||^2/(2eta_t), with no positive gradient-square term. The total bound need not be nonpositive because the initial comparator potential is positive.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"retained later target; independent approval/proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-04\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"optionalroute\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"The original BTRL15.31 contract is retained verbatim in archival_sources. Effective guarantee is repair:15.31-terminal with repair:7.47-terminal prerequisite; no unrepaired endpoint inequality is asserted.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+      \"status\": \"alternate route optional for C2 implication; already-inventoried theorem and its repair remain required/open\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          277,\n+          278\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          265,\n+          266\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\",\n+      \"scope\": {\n+        \"primary_chapter2_euclidean_implication\": \"optionalroute\",\n+        \"book_goal_required\": true,\n+        \"required_in_owning_chapter\": 15,\n+        \"scope_basis\": \"Retained source mathematics or mandatory source repair in the owning chapter; optional only as a route for the primary Chapter2 Euclidean implication. Existing source/repair distinction unchanged.\"\n+      }\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"dependency:Bregman6.4\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"Bregman6.4\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"necessarydependency\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Strictly convex psi:X->R differentiable on nonempty int X; B_psi(x;y)=psi(x)-psi(y)-<gradient psi(y),x-y>, x in X,y in int X.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"selected dependency\",\n+      \"status\": \"selected source dependency; proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          75\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          63\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Definition 6.4\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Definition 6.4Letψ:X →Rbe strictly convex and differentiable onintX ̸=∅,\\nwhereXis the domain ofψ. TheBregman divergencewith respect toψis denoted by\\nBψ :X ×intX →Rdefined as\\nBψ(x;y) :=ψ(x)−ψ(y)− ⟨∇ψ(y),x−y⟩.\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"14e499236f01b3f4ea94ea8b9071c9236cad11f749476a45eddbea02a02f2d25\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"dependency:three-point6.7\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"three-point6.7\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"necessarydependency\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"For x,y in int X,z in X: B(z;x)+B(x;y)-B(z;y)=<gradient psi(y)-gradient psi(x),z-x>.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"selected dependency\",\n+      \"status\": \"selected source dependency; proof pending\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          76\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          64\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Lemma 6.7\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Lemma 6.7(Chen and Teboulle, 1993)LetB ψ be the Bregman divergence with respect to\\nψ:X →R. Then, for any three pointsx,y∈intXandz∈ X, the following identity\\nholds\\nBψ(z;x) +B ψ(x;y)−B ψ(z;y) =⟨∇ψ(y)− ∇ψ(x),z−x⟩.\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"9b3afe81bb0ff32f56906896d77e95070476201eb493c815e83b0c67e66bbb85\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"target_id\": \"dependency:Algorithm15.9-Theorem15.31\",\n+      \"source_id\": \"Algorithm15.9-Theorem15.31\",\n+      \"scope_tag\": \"optionalroute\",\n+      \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+      \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+      \"effective_statement\": \"Effective target is repair:15.31-terminal; original retained and never silently omitted.\",\n+      \"branch\": \"selected dependency\",\n+      \"status\": \"route optional for C2 implication, retained theorem repair remains required/open\",\n+      \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+      \"source_locator\": {\n+        \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+          278,\n+          279\n+        ],\n+        \"printed_pages\": [\n+          266,\n+          267\n+        ],\n+        \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.9\",\n+        \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.9Be-the-Regularized-Leader Algorithm\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆Rd,ψ 1, . . . , ψT regularizers\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ψt(x) + Pt\\ni=1 ℓi(x)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\nwhere in the last equality we used Lemma 6.7. Dividing byη t and summing overt=\\n1, . . . , T, we have\\nTX\\nt=1\\n(ℓt(xt)−ℓ t(u))≤\\nTX\\nt=1\\n\\^RBψ(u;xt−1)\\nηt\\n− Bψ(u;xt)\\nηt\\n\\^S\\n−\\nTX\\nt=1\\nBψ(xt;xt−1)\\nηt\\n= Bψ(u;x0)\\nη1\\n− Bψ(u;xT )\\nηT\\n+\\nT−1X\\nt=1\\n\\^R 1\\nηt+1\\n− 1\\nηt\\n\\^S\\nBψ(u;xt)−\\nTX\\nt=1\\nBψ(xt;xt−1)\\nηt\\n≤ D2\\nη1\\n+D 2\\nT−1X\\nt=1\\n\\^R 1\\nηt+1\\n− 1\\nηt\\n\\^S\\n−\\nTX\\nt=1\\nBψ(xt;xt−1)\\nηt\\n= D2\\nη1\\n+D 2\\n\\^R 1\\nηT\\n− 1\\nη1\\n\\^S\\n−\\nTX\\nt=1\\nBψ(xt;xt−1)\\nηt\\n= D2\\nηT\\n−\\nTX\\nt=1\\nBψ(xt;xt−1)\\nηt\\n,\\nwhere we denoted byD 2 = max0≤t≤T−1 Bψ(u;xt).\\nThe second statement is left as an exercise.\\nThe regret of Prescient Online Mirror Descent contains the negative terms we needed\\nfrom the optimistic algorithms.\\nAnalogously, we can obtain a version of FTRL that uses the knowledge of the current\\nloss:Be-The-Regularized-Leader (BTRL), that predicts in each time step withx t ∈\\nargminx∈V ψt(x) + Pt\\ni=1 ℓi(x), see Algorithm 15.9\",\n+        \"excerpt_sha256\": \"8959c97909101e663ecee57b13505c91f6a0ad917eac09dc05452b9537e950aa\"\n+      },\n+      \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+      \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+      \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+      \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\",\n+      \"scope\": {\n+        \"primary_chapter2_euclidean_implication\": \"optionalroute\",\n+        \"book_goal_required\": true,\n+        \"required_in_owning_chapter\": 15,\n+        \"scope_basis\": \"Retained source mathematics or mandatory source repair in the owning chapter; optional only as a route for the primary Chapter2 Euclidean implication. Existing source/repair distinction unchanged.\"\n+      }\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"accepted_module_joins\": [\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientLinear.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"a7098ef90e812a20616963756f203609758ccc9701d6a30bfe0152cefe3849bc\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregman.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-causal-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"777826797a512b541d001a488899c6918f9d1404c1ba2f97811a11220648f3fc\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanRegret.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-cumulative-20261009/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"415c4c9d3e8b262afd6f849b97afad2b372a7e17233e1ac22dc8f74cc56d038d\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientBregmanSource.lean\",\n+      \"FINAL_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/FINAL-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"FINAL_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+      \"delivery_review\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-source-20261010/actual-delivery-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"delivery_verdict\": \"accepted\",\n+      \"accepted_raw_sha256\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+      \"current_raw_sha256\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+      \"git_HEAD_blob_sha256\": \"57832c9dfb4e915f9a0578ffb122792b0aac2b3404da4f6c00f2aa9fcd36bc02\",\n+      \"exact_raw_join\": true,\n+      \"exact_git_join\": true\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"candidate_gap\": \"Generic quadratic shared-Bregman identity and same actual-run Euclidean specialization of source15.30; scope adjudication before new header/proof.\",\n+  \"already_accepted\": \"Algorithm partial selector/causal run bridge and both literal conditional source15.30 bounds including fixed-step exercise.\",\n+  \"B4_remains_open\": [\n+    \"repair:7.47-terminal\",\n+    \"repair:15.31-terminal\"\n+  ],\n+  \"report_sha256\": \"4042f870981cf2c4dff9b6ac9c84aa610ebb19cf614ded7256c9b4a59d00e270\",\n+  \"inputs_unchanged\": true\n+}"},{"sha":"b2464a733c3a0a708f69dd97188b1520cc898897","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-readiness/v1.md","status":"added","additions":27,"deletions":0,"changes":27,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fv1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fv1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-readiness%2Fv1.md?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+# Prescient forward-container readiness: read-only proposal\n+\n+The existing prescient packages are independently FINAL/delivery accepted with explicit source deltas, not merely compiled helpers. All four current OnlinePrescient* modules exactly match their own accepted RAW hashes and current HEAD blobs (JSON lists each join). No old mathematical BODY rewrite is indicated by this audit.\n+\n+## Source-to-target mapping\n+\n+`forward:prescient-lookahead` is the Chapter2 PDF26 observation that current-loss access can make stability/gradient-square contributions nonpositive. The relevant Section15.5.1 is PDF277–279/printed265–267. The frozen effective lookahead family has four `later:lookahead/branch-01` through `branch-04` rows; I did not manufacture fifteen branches from “15”. Complete exact row payloads and source fingerprints are retained in JSON.\n+\n+`later:lookahead/branch-01` (Algorithm15.8): `OnlinePrescientBregman.advance` and `iterate` are the actual partial argmin selector and current-loss recursion. `advance_some_spec`, `advance_none_iff`, `iterate_prefix`, `iterate_no_recovery`, and `iterate_complete_of_step_attained` give actual choice, failure and causal semantics. `iterate_eq_of_source_updates` derives equality to the unique source update run from its actual feasible minimizers. A supplied valid run is not an arbitrary prescribed trajectory: the selector identity is proved. Current whole loss arrives before the paid state x(t+1), unlike ordinary OGD. `divergence_extension_eq` protects the ambient extension/locality boundary.\n+\n+`later:lookahead/branch-02` (Theorem15.30): accepted `source_fixed_regret` and `source_variable_regret` already transport literal source finite-domain/no-bottom/subdifferentiability and closed/strictly-convex generator assumptions into the SAME recursion, deriving properness and hseq rather than assuming them. The variable bound uses previous states t<T (source0 throughT-1), last played eta(T-1), and negative weighted movements. The fixed bound uses initial Bregman potential minus movements. The mandatory fixed-step proof left as an exercise is therefore present, not residual proof debt. Supporting accepted `iterate_fixed_sharp`/`iterate_variable_sharp` retain the terminal residual before the printed wrappers drop it by nonnegativity. Fixed T=0 is supported; the variable maximum has T>0.\n+\n+The source assumes valid argmin updates and interior iterates. General universal attainment/interior preservation is NOT justified by closedness and strict convexity alone. Keep the existing nonattainment boundary and Option failure semantics. Do not propose a false universal-existence leaf or mark conditional source wrappers incomplete just because they honestly expose validity. The source's first-order proof is replaced by the already accepted proximal comparison argument; a new constrained subgradient-sum optimality theorem is not needed merely to mimic its prose.\n+\n+`later:lookahead/branch-03` requires the Euclidean psi(z)=||z||²/2 specialization: negative sum||x_(t+1)-x_t||²/(2eta_t), with positive initial/comparator potential retained. The affine fixed-step `OnlinePrescientLinear.regret_source_bound` already proves this behavior on its own actual projected affine run, and `advance_proximal_minimizer` connects that update to its Euclidean objective. It is narrower than a generic convex/extended-loss, variable-step specialization of Algorithm15.8. Targeted search of current Online*/Tests did not locate a reusable general theorem identifying the shared `OnlineBregman.divergence` for the quadratic generator with half squared distance, or a same-run generic Euclidean specialization of both source15.30 endpoints. This is a concrete candidate gap, not a declaration-count conclusion.\n+\n+## Minimal next leaf proposal, before any new header or proof\n+\n+First adjudicate branch03's precise scope against the already accepted affine witness and generic Bregman bound. If the frozen general specialization is retained (recommended), the smallest dependency-ready producer is the shared real-inner-product quadratic Bregman identity, using the actual `divergence` and actual derivative of psi(z)=||z||²/2. Follow it with fixed and decreasing-step source-run Euclidean corollaries of the existing accepted endpoints; retain actual current-loss argmin validity/interior conditions, pre-update source centers, both exact half factors, and no blanket nonpositive total-regret claim. The identity must compute the derivative rather than accept the desired divergence equality as a premise. Existing `divergence_eq_gradient`, `three_point_identity`, `divergence_nonneg` and the source endpoints are available implementation dependencies. Exact mathlib derivative producer retrieval and proposed header roundtrip are next planning steps, not performed proof work or frozen new API here. For psi on all E, interior is all E; retain feasible-set and loss assumptions. No duplicate prescient recursion/project is needed.\n+\n+If a distinct source adjudication finds the existing affine actual-run witness sufficient for the primary Chapter2 “can” observation, that could resolve only that primary implication by reconciliation. It does not silently discharge the frozen generic branch03 or its owning source obligations. Conversely, do not perpetually label branch02 missing after inspecting its accepted exact terminals.\n+\n+## B4 and ownership\n+\n+`later:lookahead/branch-04` and `dependency:Algorithm15.9-Theorem15.31` explicitly retain the BTRL alternative and its source repair. They are optional only as the route for the primary C2 Euclidean implication, while the inventoried theorem remains required in owning Chapter15. `repair:15.31-terminal` and its prerequisite `repair:7.47-terminal` remain genuinely open under B4. The proposed ghost x_(T+1)=x_T/unhinted final convention, finite-value scope and separate extended-value branches are qualified corrections, not an equivalent reading of repeating the last loss/hint. Never transfer Algorithm15.30 acceptance to this different algorithm or discard the original offending terminal. No BTRL proof/header is started here.\n+\n+The Bregman definition and three-point dependency rows have candidate exact shared implementations; their own separate source-row reconciliation is not inferred from accepted consumers. No chapter status/count/denominator change, no source-container acceptance, no canonical/root/site/native writes and no builds. The artifacts are a source-exposed independent readiness audit, not a blind review. PDF bytes were rehashed and pages26,277–279 extracted directly with pypdf. No fresh pixel inspection was performed; formulas were crosschecked against the frozen exact rows and current source. Initial fitz imports failed because unavailable; pypdf extraction succeeded without installing packages."},{"sha":"b9ace0239af77b6efdc988da6ececa7a928b1e4c","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-26-text.txt","status":"added","additions":137,"deletions":0,"changes":137,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-26-text.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-26-text.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-26-text.txt?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,137 @@\n+14Online Subgradient Descent\n+have\n+TX\n+t=1\n+(ℓt(xt)−ℓ t(u))≤\n+TX\n+t=1\n+^R ∥xt −u∥ 2\n+2\n+2ηt\n+− ∥xt+1 −u∥ 2\n+2\n+2ηt\n+^S\n++\n+TX\n+t=1\n+ηt∥gt∥2\n+2\n+2\n+= ∥x1 −u∥ 2\n+2\n+2η1\n+− ∥xT+1 −u∥ 2\n+2\n+2ηT\n++\n+T−1X\n+t=1\n+^R 1\n+ηt+1\n+− 1\n+ηt\n+^S ∥xt+1 −u∥ 2\n+2\n+2 +\n+TX\n+t=1\n+ηt∥gt∥2\n+2\n+2\n+≤ D2\n+2η1\n++ D2\n+2\n+T−1X\n+t=1\n+^R 1\n+ηt+1\n+− 1\n+ηt\n+^S\n++\n+TX\n+t=1\n+ηt∥gt∥2\n+2\n+2 − ∥xT+1 −u∥ 2\n+2\n+2ηT\n+= D2\n+2η1\n++D 2\n+^R 1\n+2ηT\n+− 1\n+2η1\n+^S\n++\n+TX\n+t=1\n+ηt∥gt∥2\n+2\n+2 − ∥xT+1 −u∥ 2\n+2\n+2ηT\n+= D2\n+2ηT\n++\n+TX\n+t=1\n+ηt\n+2 ∥gt∥2\n+2 − 1\n+2ηT\n+∥xT+1 −u∥ 2\n+2 .\n+In the same way, whenη t is constant, we have\n+TX\n+t=1\n+(ℓt(xt)−ℓ t(u))≤\n+TX\n+t=1\n+^R 1\n+2η ∥xt −u∥ 2\n+2 − 1\n+2η ∥xt+1 −u∥ 2\n+2\n+^S\n++ η\n+2\n+TX\n+t=1\n+∥gt∥2\n+2\n+= 1\n+2η ∥x1 −u∥ 2\n+2 − 1\n+2η ∥xT+1 −u∥ 2\n+2 + η\n+2\n+TX\n+t=1\n+∥gt∥2\n+2 .\n+We can immediately observe a few things.\n+•The terms∥g t∥2\n+2 are due to the fact that we outputx t before knowing the lossℓ t. Indeed,\n+these terms become non-positive if we were allowed to observeℓ t before producingx t,\n+see Section 15.5.1.\n+•In the case of constantη, the bound holds even whenD=∞. Moreover, the first term in\n+the regret depends on ourinitial condition, that is, how farx 1 is from the competitoru.\n+•The last term in both bounds is non-positive, so it is usually discarded. Yet, some advanced\n+proofs require it, so it is good to be aware of it.\n+•If we want to use time-varying learning rates, we need to control the terms∥x t −u∥ 2\n+2. To\n+do it, we assume a bounded domainV. However, this assumption is false in most of the\n+machine learning applications. We will also see in Section 5.2 that this is not an artifact of\n+the proof, that is, OGD can fail in unbounded domains with time-varying learning rates.\n+That said, in the stochastic setting, you can still use a time-varying learning rate in SGD\n+with an unbounded domain, as we will see in Chapter 3.\n+•Another important observation is that the regret bound helps us choose the learning rates\n+ηt. Indeed, it is the only guideline we have. Any other choice that is not justified by a\n+regret analysis is not justified at all.\n+As we said, the presence of untuned parameters like the learning rates makes no sense in\n+online learning. So, we have to decide on a strategy to set them. A simple choice is to find\n+the constant learning rate that minimizes the bounds for a fixed number of iterations. We\n\\ No newline at end of file"},{"sha":"62467be19cfcf76fc66abc56f7640332a76ccc83","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-26.png","status":"added","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-26.png","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-26.png","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-26.png?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6"},{"sha":"8a021147650d082f37485dddb72ed965ddfdd002","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-277-text.txt","status":"added","additions":60,"deletions":0,"changes":60,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-277-text.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-277-text.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-277-text.txt?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+15.5 Faster Rates Through Optimism265\n+Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\n+Require:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\n+differentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\n+1:fort= 1toTdo\n+2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\n+3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\n+ηt\n+Bψ(x;x t−1)\n+4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\n+5:end for\n+15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\n+The results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\n+cause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\n+tion”. However, if we only care about converging to the saddle point without worrying about\n+communication, we can easily do better. For example, we can use the fact that it is fine if\n+one of the two players “cheats” by looking at the loss at the beginning of each round, mak-\n+ing its regret non-positive, while the other uses optimistic updates. However, as discussed\n+in Remark 15.16, this will change the oracle, because now one of the algorithms needs to\n+access the functions rather than only their gradients.\n+For example, we saw the use of best response. However, best response only guarantees\n+non-positive regret, while for the optimistic proof above we need some specific negative\n+terms. It turns out we can achieve them with another algorithm:Prescient Online Mirror\n+Descent, that predicts in each round withx t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\n+ηt\n+Bψ(x;x t−1), see\n+Algorithm 15.8.\n+Theorem 15.30Letψ:X →Rdifferentiable inintX, closed, and strictly convex. Let\n+V ⊆ Xbe a non-empty closed convex set. Assumex t ∈intX,ℓ t subdifferentiable onV,\n+andη t+1 ≤η t, fort= 1, . . . , T. Then,∀u∈ V, Algorithm 15.8 satisfies\n+TX\n+t=1\n+ℓt(xt)−\n+TX\n+t=1\n+ℓt(u)≤max\n+0≤t≤T−1\n+Bψ(u;x t)\n+ηT\n+−\n+TX\n+t=1\n+1\n+ηt\n+Bψ(xt;x t−1).\n+Moreover, ifη t is constant, i.e.,η t =η∀t= 1, . . . , T, we have\n+TX\n+t=1\n+(ℓt(xt)−ℓ t(u))≤ Bψ(u;x 0)\n+η − 1\n+η\n+TX\n+t=1\n+Bψ(xt;x t−1).\n+ProofFrom the first-order optimality condition of Theorem 2.8 on the update, we have\n+that there existsg t ∈∂ℓ t(xt)such that\n+⟨ηtgt +∇ψ(x t)− ∇ψ(x t−1),u−x t⟩ ≥0,∀u∈ V.\n+Hence, we have\n+ηt(ℓt(xt)−ℓ t(u))≤ ⟨η tgt,x t −u⟩ ≤ ⟨∇ψ(x t−1)− ∇ψ(x t),x t −u⟩\n+=B ψ(u;x t−1)−B ψ(u;x t)−B ψ(xt;x t−1),\n\\ No newline at end of file"},{"sha":"254caea7cac52d23dd4db808a13d46ae5bdafddb","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-277.png","status":"added","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-277.png","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-277.png","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-277.png?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6"},{"sha":"3867458c928abd0302e0e8edb2cf1b04345d47c1","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-278-text.txt","status":"added","additions":93,"deletions":0,"changes":93,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-278-text.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-278-text.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-278-text.txt?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@\n+266Saddle-Point Optimization and Online Algorithms\n+Algorithm 15.9Be-the-Regularized-Leader Algorithm\n+Require:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ 1, . . . , ψT regularizers\n+1:fort= 1toTdo\n+2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\n+3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ψt(x) +Pt\n+i=1 ℓi(x)\n+4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\n+5:end for\n+where in the last equality we used Lemma 6.7. Dividing byη t and summing overt=\n+1, . . . , T, we have\n+TX\n+t=1\n+(ℓt(xt)−ℓ t(u))≤\n+TX\n+t=1\n+^R Bψ(u;x t−1)\n+ηt\n+− Bψ(u;x t)\n+ηt\n+^S\n+−\n+TX\n+t=1\n+Bψ(xt;x t−1)\n+ηt\n+= Bψ(u;x 0)\n+η1\n+− Bψ(u;x T )\n+ηT\n++\n+T−1X\n+t=1\n+^R 1\n+ηt+1\n+− 1\n+ηt\n+^S\n+Bψ(u;x t)−\n+TX\n+t=1\n+Bψ(xt;x t−1)\n+ηt\n+≤ D2\n+η1\n++D 2\n+T−1X\n+t=1\n+^R 1\n+ηt+1\n+− 1\n+ηt\n+^S\n+−\n+TX\n+t=1\n+Bψ(xt;x t−1)\n+ηt\n+= D2\n+η1\n++D 2\n+^R 1\n+ηT\n+− 1\n+η1\n+^S\n+−\n+TX\n+t=1\n+Bψ(xt;x t−1)\n+ηt\n+= D2\n+ηT\n+−\n+TX\n+t=1\n+Bψ(xt;x t−1)\n+ηt\n+,\n+where we denoted byD 2 = max0≤t≤T−1 Bψ(u;x t).\n+The second statement is left as an exercise.\n+The regret of Prescient Online Mirror Descent contains the negative terms we needed\n+from the optimistic algorithms.\n+Analogously, we can obtain a version of FTRL that uses the knowledge of the current\n+loss:Be-The-Regularized-Leader (BTRL), that predicts in each time step withx t ∈\n+argminx∈V ψt(x) +Pt\n+i=1 ℓi(x), see Algorithm 15.9.\n+Ifψ t ≡0, then Be-The-Regularized-Leader becomes theBe-The-Leaderalgorithm.\n+BTRL can be thought of as Optimistic FTRL where ˜ℓt =ℓ t. Hence, from the regret of\n+Optimistic FTRL in Theorem 7.47, we immediately have the following theorem.\n+Theorem 15.31LetV ⊂R d be convex, closed, and non-empty. Assume fort= 1, . . . , T\n+thatψ t +Pt\n+i=1 ℓi is proper, closed, andλ t-strongly convex with respect to∥ · ∥. Then, for\n\\ No newline at end of file"},{"sha":"5248ecacd713ea1704c22b6d3e12204e7f176e1d","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-278.png","status":"added","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-278.png","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-278.png","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fsource-topology-proposal-v1%2Fsource-278.png?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6"},{"sha":"49553965e97bb449ae234cb3306aff31c1882e5d","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-p